@page "/privacy"
@page "/privacy-policy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - ENVIMIX project</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <MetadataTags Title="Privacy Policy - ENVIMIX project"
                  Description="Read how the ENVIMIX project collects, uses, and protects account and gameplay data."></MetadataTags>
</HeadContent>

<ReuContainer>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="legal-document">
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: 8 September 2026</p>

        <h2>1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
            ENVIMIX project ("the Service," "we," "us," or "our") is a community-driven platform for TrackMania and ManiaPlanet players that provides record tracking, leaderboards, registered-server and session information, and title pack distribution services.
        </p>
        <p>
            The Service is part of the gbx.tools ecosystem and relies on <a href="https://identity.gbx.tools">identity.gbx.tools</a> for user authentication and identity management. We do not operate our own account system and do not store credentials.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Authentication and Data Access</h2>
        <p>
            When you sign in on envimix.gbx.tools, we use a secure, shared authentication cookie issued by identity.gbx.tools to verify your identity. This cookie is essential and we may use it to request additional data from the identity manager as needed to provide functionality.
        </p>
        <p>
            All identity-related data processing, including OAuth provider data, cookies, and account management, is governed by the <a href="https://identity.gbx.tools/privacy">identity.gbx.tools Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Data We Store</h2>
        
        <h3>3.1 Player Data</h3>
        <p>
            To provide record tracking and leaderboard services, we store limited data received from identity.gbx.tools:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>User ID (for account association)</li>
            <li>ManiaPlanet login, nickname, zone, avatar URL, language, profile description, colour, Steam user ID, and game profile statistics made available to the Service</li>
            <li>Discord account ID, username, nickname, and avatar information when linked to the Service</li>
            <li>Account creation, update, authorization-interest, and moderation status information</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3.2 Game Records</h3>
        <p>
            When you play on registered servers or submit records, we store:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Race times, scores, respawns, lap count, gravity setting, and checkpoint data</li>
            <li>Map, campaign, title pack, author, vehicle, and medal information</li>
            <li>Ghost data for verification</li>
            <li>Gameplay, submission, session, and source-server timestamps and identifiers</li>
            <li>Record status and history, including validation, world-record, removal, and restoration status</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3.3 Server Data</h3>
        <p>
            For registered dedicated servers, we maintain:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Server login, display name, registration time, deletion status, and moderation status</li>
            <li>The account that registered a server and the server's session, mode, map, title, start, expiry, and end information</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3.4 Service Operation Data</h3>
        <p>
            We store title pack versions, downloadable map and title pack data, and identifiers for Discord messages created by the Service so that those messages can be managed when appropriate.
        </p>

        <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
        <p>
            We use collected data to:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Maintain leaderboards and player rankings</li>
            <li>Verify record authenticity and prevent cheating</li>
            <li>Enable server integration and API services</li>
            <li>Improve service performance and user experience</li>
            <li>Ensure fair play and community standards</li>
            <li>Administer server registration, session operation, record moderation, and title pack access</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>
            We may share data in the following circumstances:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Publicly displaying leaderboards, validators, player profiles, records, record status, map and title information, registered servers, and sessions</li>
            <li>Publishing Envimix Turbo validation, world-record, record-removal, and record-restoration notices through Discord webhooks; these notices may include player, map, vehicle, record time, and event-time information</li>
            <li>When required by law or to protect our rights</li>
            <li>With your explicit consent</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Player records, leaderboard data, and related server and session information are publicly visible as part of the competitive gaming experience. Discord processes webhook content under its own policies.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>
            Deleting your account through identity.gbx.tools will restrict your access to the Service, but some game-related data will continue being stored to maintain leaderboard integrity. This includes:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Historical records, race times, ghost data, checkpoints, and record status history</li>
            <li>User ID from identity manager (anonymized reference)</li>
            <li>ManiaPlanet login, nickname, zone, and other public profile data used for record attribution</li>
            <li>Server registration and session data, including its association with the registering account (if applicable)</li>
            <li>Discord message identifiers required to manage published notices</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            After account deletion, you cannot manage this data until creating a new account that can associate to this data. You have the right to request complete data deletion or remove server integrations by contacting us.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
            We implement appropriate security measures to protect your information:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Encrypted connections (HTTPS) for all data transmission</li>
            <li>Secure storage of authentication tokens and sensitive data</li>
            <li>Regular security monitoring and updates</li>
            <li>Access controls and API rate limiting</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>
            Your data protection rights, including GDPR rights where applicable, are described in the <a href="https://identity.gbx.tools/privacy">identity.gbx.tools Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            Additionally, you can contact us for data deletion requests.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Updates to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our services or legal requirements. Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
            For questions about this Privacy Policy or data deletion requests, please contact us through the <a href="https://discord.envimix.gbx.tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nadeo Envimix Discord server</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</ReuContainer>
